+// Dark pop landing assist ("contact assist"). A recording of 38 dark pop attempts showed the game raises a
+// package of flags in the skater's request block on the tick before it bails (the dismount request at
+// context+0x13d4 bit 0x100 and three others, see no_bail.cpp) and never in an attempt that popped. While
+// enabled, once D-pad Right (the menu) has been down at any point in the current flight, those flags are cleared
+// on the tick the landing stage shows, so the game judges the pop first; the latch resets when the skater is back
+// on the ground. When the game then chooses the pop by itself, the wipeout it asks for on the next ticks, and the
+// dismount it asks for when that flight lands, are held off (the same swap No Bail does) for 4 s, at most 0.4 s at a
+// time, and the bail flags are cleared in that window too.
+// Publish from the client tick.
+void contact_assist_update(bool enabled, bool dpad_down) noexcept;
+std::uint64_t contact_assist_count() noexcept; // times the flags were cleared since the process started
+std::uint64_t contact_assist_holds() noexcept; // wipeouts held off during a pop since the process started
+unsigned contact_assist_last_mask() noexcept; // which of the four were set the last time (bit 0..3)
 // Stopping flight must not discard the independent manual preference.
 void clear_no_bail_flight() noexcept;
 }
